  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A tin chloride <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> undergoes the following reactions (not balanced)<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is a monoanion having pyramidal geometry. Both <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> are neutral compounds. Choose the correct option(s).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "boufy",
      "text": "The central atoms in X is  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>  hybridized",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gjMBf",
      "text": "The oxidation state of the central atom in  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>  is  <math><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hFfCA",
      "text": "The central atom in  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>  has one lone pair of electrons",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vk71w",
      "text": "There is a coordinate bond in  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sn has vacant d orbitals in tin(II)chloride which can be used to accommodate electron pairs and form coordinate bond.</p><p>LP = Lone pairs</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/273ea66c-d5d9-4dbf-93a4-7ec020fb4898-image.png\"/></p><p>X is mono anion with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridisation and It has trigonal pyramidal geometry.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/76fe5720-bb88-4389-8c1a-c68662675b59-image.png\"/></p><p>The above reaction is a Lewis acid-base reaction. The adduct Y formed is a coordination compound, and it is a neutral compound.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/e0e9f259-8c8a-4b31-af61-45010bc9e0f1-image.png\"/></p><p>The central atom in Z is tin, its oxidation state is +4, and it has no lone pair electrons. Z is a neutral compound.</p><p> </p>",
    "image": null
  },
